# dsh-tasksuite — example HOST composition fragment (cordis.yml)
#
# When you want the supervisor to run for *every* session in a DSH deployment
# (not just one preset), add its plugin row to the host `cordis.yml` alongside
# the existing registries. Because awr-goal-supervisor only consumes host
# services (`shell`, `timer`) and publishes none, it can safely live in the host
# plane — this is the deployment-grade placement. The awr-tools / awr-task-board
# rows are better left to a preset that needs them.
#
# This file is illustrative; merge the relevant rows into your real cordis.yml.

plugins:
  # --- Outer scheduling loop, process-wide -------------------------------
  - id: awr-goal-supervisor
    name: /home/wdf-pai/kf/dsh-tasksuite/plugins/awr-goal-supervisor/index.js
    config:
      awrBin: awr
      workdir: /home/wdf-pai/kf
      projectArg: /home/wdf-pai/kf
      stalenessMs: 120000
      heartbeatMs: 30000
      dryRun: false

  # --- OS-layer watchdog reasoning (README): cron + systemd ------------------
  # The supervisor detects fake-death and prints a STALE/FAKE-DEATH marker on
  # stdout. A cron/systemd unit watches that marker and, on restart, launches a
  # fresh root agent via dsh-headless which runs `awr recovery` + resume. That
  # OS layer is NOT part of this plugin; it belongs in your deployment unit.
